1
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:07,298
<i>- Welcome!</i>
<i>- Welcome!</i>

2
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,718
<i>Welcome</i>

3
00:00:09,801 --> 00:00:12,137
<i>- Welcome!</i>
<i>- Welcome!</i>

4
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:14,764
- All right. You can come out now.
- Okay.

5
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:15,890
Sorry about that.

6
00:00:15,974 --> 00:00:16,975
POURING OUT

7
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:18,435
They're also guests.

8
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:20,311
Our boss will give an introduction.

9
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,022
Do it like a docent.

10
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:24,107
- Hello. Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

11
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,526
I'm the owner of Kian's B&B, Kian84.

12
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:27,861
And they're our employees.

13
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:29,612
- Yeon-koung.
- Hello.

14
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,909
- Kazuha.
- Hello.

15
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,621
- And finally, Jun-ho.
- Hello.

16
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:39,706
How are you?

17
00:00:40,373 --> 00:00:42,375
- Hello.
- This is awesome.

18
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:43,793
And…

19
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,296
BRAIN RESETS

20
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:48,715
First of all…

21
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:49,632
Go ahead.

22
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:53,136
We should show them the facilities
you worked really hard to prepare.

23
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:55,013
- Like what?
- They're all here, so… Like what?

24
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,347
Facilities?

25
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:58,850
WE SHOULD SHOW THEM AROUND

26
00:00:58,933 --> 00:00:59,768
Sorry, Jun-ho.

27
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,686
- It's okay.
- I spent a lot of energy earlier.

28
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,772
THEY FOLLOW THE DOCENT

29
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:07,067
THIS PLACE IS…

30
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,736
It's so efficient.

31
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,322
LAUNDRY ROOM?

32
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:14,699
We're actually drying
the laundry right now.

33
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,993
- It's a sauna.
- It's really nice.

34
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:18,495
It's warm.

35
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:20,038
And let me explain one more thing.

36
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:25,460
And this place is for you
to manage your health.

37
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,836
It's a gym.

38
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:30,799
And this TV is…
Could you all gather in front?

39
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:32,509
Please come to the front of the TV.

40
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:34,344
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

41
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,637
Hey, it's a karaoke room.

42
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,056
Nice.

43
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:39,140
BRAVO

44
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:40,600
- That's so cool.
- Everyone.

45
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:44,270
If each of you doesn't sing
at least one song before you check out,

46
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,438
you can't check out.

47
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:48,066
- Yes. Got it?
- Yes.

48
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,569
THE DOCENT FINISHES SHOWING THEM AROUND

49
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:53,154
Now, the rooms.

50
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:54,864
Which one did you choose?

51
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,157
Up there.

52
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,992
THEY CHOSE THE WINDOWSILL

53
00:01:58,076 --> 00:01:59,744
- What about you?
- We'll go here.

54
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:00,954
THEY CHOSE THE TV CABINET

55
00:02:01,037 --> 00:02:01,955
Good.

56
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:03,081
Let's sleep in the fridge.

57
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,582
It'll be easier for us to climb up.

58
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:05,917
- All three of you?
- Yes.

59
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,794
THEY CHOSE THE FRIDGE

60
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:10,004
Now, we'll have
a comforter presentation ceremony.

61
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:13,174
Rather than a presentation ceremony,
you have to take them yourselves.

62
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:14,968
But they're so big.

63
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:18,513
- Can we just climb up?
- Yes, that's fine.

64
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,849
Do as you please.
You can get on each other's shoulders.

65
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,321
THEY CLIMB UP

66
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,115
SO EASILY

67
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:39,075
- What do you need?
- Which one…

68
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,035
- The yellow one, please.
- Okay.

69
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:43,621
Thank you.

70
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:47,500
It's so heavy.

71
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:48,668
You're right.

72
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:51,171
THEY CAN EVEN ORGANIZE THE HANGERS

73
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:53,089
Is it supposed to be that easy?

74
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:55,717
- What on earth?
- They're so good.

75
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,594
CURIOUS ABOUT WHO THEY ARE

76
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,640
They must have great core strength.

77
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:05,727
- Do you do rock climbing?
- Yes.

78
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:07,729
- You're climbers.
- Climbing.

79
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,022
We do ice climbing.

80
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:10,732
We're professional ice climbers.

81
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:24,037
- Complete!
- Descending.

82
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:27,957
NATIONAL TEAM, KIM MIN-CHEOL

83
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:31,419
NATIONAL TEAM, PARK JOON-KYU

84
00:03:33,671 --> 00:03:35,381
NATIONAL TEAM, LEE YOUNG-GEON

85
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:36,925
- You're athletes?
- Yes.

86
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:38,301
- Their forearms are huge.
- Right.

87
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:39,928
- You're right.
- Look at their forearms.

88
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:42,222
We'd been in a competition
up until yesterday.

89
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:43,890
- National Sports Festival?
- Yes.

90
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:45,308
Different from the winter one?

91
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:46,392
A WINTER SPORT LIKE LUGE

92
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:47,894
- Is it the same as the others?
- Yes.

93
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:49,812
We had the luge team stay with us before.

94
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:51,773
So how did it go?

95
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:53,233
First, second, and third place.

96
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,943
- In the individual event?
- Amazing.

97
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,862
First, second, and third?

98
00:03:57,946 --> 00:03:59,155
We'll prepare dinner now.

99
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,699
- Zuha, will it take long?
- Yes, if I'm starting now.

100
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:03,409
What do we do?

101
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:04,661
Boss will help.

102
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:07,163
- You're going to help me, right?
- Yeah.

103
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:12,585
JUN-HO GOES TO HELP TOO

104
00:04:13,836 --> 00:04:16,256
- I don't think I can climb this anymore.
- Right?

105
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:17,423
Seriously, I can't.

106
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:19,425
- It exhausts your arms, doesn't it?
- Yeah.

107
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:25,181
Why is the volleyball here?

108
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,100
That ball? It bounced up here.

109
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,437
TRACE OF DAZZLING VOLLEYBALL PERFORMANCE

110
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:33,648
- Could you take this, please?
- Sure.

111
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:37,318
It's wet.

112
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:39,153
Here are the wet wipes.

113
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:40,697
YEON-KOUNG IS HELPING GUESTS

114
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,533
I think I've seen you before.

115
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:45,076
- Me?
- Yes. No?

116
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,452
No.

117
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:47,787
<i>Physical: 100.</i>

118
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,416
That's why you looked familiar.

119
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:54,294
I thought I'd seen you
at the National Training Center.

120
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,463
We haven't been able to train there yet.

121
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:59,632
- Why not?
- It's not an official Olympic sport.

122
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,175
- Really?
- Yes.

123
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:04,095
Now, I'm starting to feel a bit hungry.

124
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,388
Are you hungry?

125
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,765
We have a few snacks here.

126
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:08,975
Sweet potatoes too.

127
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:10,810
THEY'RE ALL HUNGRY

128
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:12,395
Zuha, how long will it take?

129
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:13,354
An hour and a half?

130
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:14,939
Then, assume it'll take two hours.

131
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:17,191
What? That's too long.

132
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:18,735
We'll try an hour and a half then.

133
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:19,986
They said they're hungry.

134
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:21,279
What do we do?

135
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:23,364
- We have to make Hamburg steak.
- Hamburg steak.

136
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:25,325
- And <i>Napolitan.</i>
- Right, <i>Napolitan.</i>

137
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:26,617
These go in the Hamburg steak.

138
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,870
Then, should I mince them finely?

139
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:30,872
Thin like what is used in pasta.

140
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:33,166
- Cut the bell peppers thinly too?
- Yes.

141
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:35,293
IN CHARGE OF HAMBURG STEAK INGREDIENTS

142
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:42,508
KNIFE SKILLS LIKE NANTA

143
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,260
IN CHARGE OF NAPOLITAN INGREDIENTS

144
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:46,512
WITH A FRUIT KNIFE

145
00:05:47,346 --> 00:05:49,515
DELICATELY AS IF SCULPTING

146
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:51,225
Zuha, is this good enough?

147
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:53,144
- My eyes are burning.
- Yes.

148
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:56,230
I'm sure I can do this.

149
00:05:57,231 --> 00:05:58,399
BREAD CRUMBS

150
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,359
MILK

151
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:03,237
PORK

152
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:05,114
BEEF

153
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,574
ONIONS

154
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:10,661
THE HAMBURG STEAK MIX IS READY

155
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:11,621
5:30 P.M.

156
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:13,122
Do you need help up there?

157
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:14,665
Up here?

158
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,959
Is it going to take a while?

159
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:17,877
A little bit.

160
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:20,171
- They said they were really hungry.
- Oh, no.

161
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:23,382
Cut that one, and it should be enough.

162
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:24,884
- Stop here? Okay.
- Yes.

163
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:27,095
- You feel rushed, don't you?
- Yes.

164
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:30,515
I mean, we always started cooking
before the guests arrived.

165
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:31,724
Right.

166
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,810
It's hard because we started
after they all came.

167
00:06:33,893 --> 00:06:34,894
Right?

168
00:06:34,977 --> 00:06:37,105
I think you can start at 4:00 p.m.

169
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:44,112
FAST

170
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:46,364
You're julienning better
than you did yesterday.

171
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:48,282
I realized how to do it.

172
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:49,659
We're getting better.

173
00:06:49,742 --> 00:06:50,993
Right.

174
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:53,121
- And these things are all new to us.
- Yeah.

175
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:54,914
- Isn't it a bit stuffy?
- Yeah.

176
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:57,959
Gosh, it's so heavy.

177
00:06:58,042 --> 00:06:59,710
Wait. I can't get down if it's open.

178
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,462
The distance becomes much greater.

179
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,923
Hey, this is way too open.

180
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:04,966
TOO OPEN

181
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:06,634
This spot has a great view.

182
00:07:06,717 --> 00:07:09,220
Come up here. The view's nice.

183
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,392
I wonder what else there is.

184
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:15,518
Nice view.

185
00:07:15,601 --> 00:07:17,687
IT HAS A GREAT VIEW

186
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,313
I'm Kim Jun-yeop.

187
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:20,606
And I'm Lee In-beom.

188
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:21,816
THEY INTRODUCE THEMSELVES

189
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:24,569
- What are your names?
- Should we go over there too?

190
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,529
- This spot is a bit…
- We'll come down.

191
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,949
THEY'RE ALL GATHERED

192
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,701
I am Ground…

193
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:33,536
SEATING ARRANGEMENT
CALLS FOR PARTY GAMES

194
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,663
- This way!
- This way!

195
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:36,873
COMPELLED TO START

196
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:37,790
I'm Park Joon-kyu.

197
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,208
I'm Kim Jun-yeop.

198
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,627
- I'm Lee In-beom.
- This is too much.

199
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:43,337
The two of us are a bit older, so…

200
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:44,672
LEARNING NAMES OVER FOR REAL

201
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:46,716
LEE IN-BEOM, KIM JUN-YEOP

202
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:48,259
PARK JOON-KYU

203
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:50,761
LEE YOUNG-GEON, KIM MIN-CHEOL

204
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:52,805
CHOI A-RIN, CHOI A-JIN

205
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:53,848
Siblings?

206
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:55,224
- Sisters.
- Right.

207
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:57,059
Siblings? Who is the brother?

208
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,565
Kian, look over there.

209
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:03,941
Look at them.

210
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,818
- My goodness.
- They're all together.

211
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,570
- This is a first.
- It is.

212
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:08,738
It's what you wanted.

213
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:10,656
That's what I drew in my initial plans.

214
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,200
They must be introducing themselves.

215
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:16,329
They're behaving as we planned
because we welcomed them properly.

216
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:17,955
- Yeah.
- They don't feel awkward.

217
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,123
I bet they don't.

218
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,833
A warm welcome makes a huge impact.

219
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:23,461
- We did it three times.
- Yeah, I think it's good.

220
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,171
Are the girls college students?

221
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:26,839
They resemble each other.

222
00:08:26,923 --> 00:08:28,841
- They're sisters. Yeah.
- Right?

223
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:31,219
- I wonder what job the ponytail guy has.
- Right?

224
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:32,803
I bet there's a story behind it.

225
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:33,721
- A story?
- A story?

226
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:35,932
Maybe he donates it?

227
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:37,141
- His hair?
- By cutting it?

228
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:38,768
THEY SUDDENLY BEGIN GUESSING

229
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:41,812
Well, I was thinking
he might be in a rock band.

230
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:42,813
A ROCKER?

231
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,815
Rock band guys these days
don't have long hair.

232
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,442
He doesn't seem like one though.

233
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,069
To me, he seems like

234
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:50,488
someone who does mind-body practice.

235
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:52,406
A successor to his master's practice.

236
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,867
You sure do have a lot of unique thoughts.

237
00:08:55,701 --> 00:08:57,036
TOO BUSY TO LISTEN

238
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:01,290
Could you shape the patties for me?

239
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,084
- Make them round? Okay.
- The Hamburg steak.

240
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:05,044
- We should make them small.
- Let's do that.

241
00:09:05,127 --> 00:09:06,796
- Like mini patties.
- Yes, mini.

242
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:09,131
- Round like this?
- Yes.

243
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:10,341
How is this?

244
00:09:10,841 --> 00:09:12,260
You look pretty cool.

245
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:16,055
While you do that,
we'll hurry up and cook them.

246
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:17,473
Like this?

247
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:19,267
Yes.

248
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,269
We can cook them a bit more.

249
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,063
They look so good.

250
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,110
I mean, Zuha's food is the best.
It always has been.

251
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:30,861
Yeah, her food is always good.

252
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,823
I haven't done this very often.

253
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:35,449
SHE STARTS MAKING THE NAPOLITAN

254
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:37,159
Did I put in too many ingredients?

255
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:39,370
THE PAN IS ALREADY FULL WITHOUT THE PASTA

256
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,789
You have to control portion sizes
to look like a good cook.

257
00:09:41,872 --> 00:09:43,624
If you don't,
you look like a bad cook.

258
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:45,501
A lot of cow feed
was left over yesterday.

259
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:47,044
Geez, that's making me mad.

260
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:48,879
<i>There was more left over than my pizza.</i>

261
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,214
YEON-KOUNG'S LEFTOVER FOOD

262
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:53,009
I'm taking some consolation from that.

263
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,093
Gosh, I'm so angry.

264
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,262
Don't worry. I'll eat it all.

265
00:09:57,346 --> 00:09:58,598
Yeah, I will too.

266
00:09:58,681 --> 00:09:59,765
Except for Boss's.

267
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,350
Don't worry.

268
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,936
The pasta will be done
sooner than expected.

269
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:05,980
It's hot!

270
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:09,400
ADDING KETCHUP

271
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:12,820
Hold on. It takes a lot of ketchup.

272
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:15,448
A LOT OF KETCHUP

273
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:19,493
- Zuha.
- That looks good.

274
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:21,537
- Yes?
- I think they'll love this.

275
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,872
Yay.

276
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:24,957
- You'll become the cooking goddess.
- Exactly.

277
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,751
THE COOKING GODDESS'S FINAL TOUCH

278
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:30,171
Is that right?

279
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:32,673
Was that on purpose?

280
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:35,009
Let's just say it's right.
But a lot does go in.

281
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:37,845
- Really?
- So it should be all right.

282
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,472
Those cooked really well.

283
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:41,557
- Are these all right?
- They look good.

284
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:44,810
Jun-ho cooks well.
He didn't burn any of his pizzas either.

285
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:47,980
- Is this what you envisioned?
- Yes.

286
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:49,732
- Yeah?
- They look so good.

287
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:51,484
- Should we bring these down?
- Sure.

288
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:52,401
- Are you done?
- Yes.

289
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:53,569
TIME TO BRING THE FOOD DOWN

290
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:55,446
Could you help us with this?

291
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:56,739
Sure.

292
00:10:56,822 --> 00:10:57,823
Thank you.

293
00:10:57,907 --> 00:10:59,533
We'll get ready to eat now.

294
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:00,701
TRAYS BROUGHT DOWN FIRST

295
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,787
- I got it. You got the other end?
- Okay.

296
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,872
Gosh, it looks so good.

297
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,500
It's hot. Be careful.

298
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:10,586
Hamburg steaks!

299
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:14,048
JUN-HO & THE BOSS COME DOWN TO EAT TOO

300
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:16,592
AND TODAY'S CHEF ZUHA TOO

301
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:17,885
This looks amazing.

302
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:19,178
HAMBURG STEAK & NAPOLITAN

303
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:22,390
Zuha cooked these.
Could you tell us about your dishes?

304
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:26,435
I made <i>Napolitan</i> and some Hamburg steaks.

305
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:30,022
I started ballet
when I was three years old.

306
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:31,899
And I went abroad to learn it.

307
00:11:31,982 --> 00:11:33,275
Where did you go?

308
00:11:33,359 --> 00:11:34,860
I went to the Netherlands.

309
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:36,487
ZUHA STUDIED BALLET IN THE NETHERLANDS

310
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,906
So you ate these dishes often there.

311
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:42,535
Yes, we made these often back then,
so I wanted to introduce them to you.

312
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:45,287
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

313
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:48,165
And everyone, one more thing…

314
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:50,918
Before you start to eat,

315
00:11:51,001 --> 00:11:54,422
if you could choose
an employee you'd like to eat with…

316
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:55,673
EXCITED, FEELING PRESSURE

317
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:58,259
You can eat and chat with that employee.

318
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:01,011
We'll get to know each other
faster that way too.

319
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:03,431
And we'll all get together later
after dinner anyway.

320
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:06,392
So, please choose the employee
you'd like to eat with.

321
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,018
No pressure.

322
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:09,019
All right?

323
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,396
- Okay.
- Okay.

324
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:11,814
Should we turn around? Or…

325
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:13,524
- Should we do that?
- Let's turn around.

326
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:16,402
Let's make it quick.
The pasta will get mushy.

327
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,945
I don't think anyone will pick me.

328
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,239
I've never been picked before, so…

329
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:22,867
We were so torn.

330
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,076
No, it's really all right.

331
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,161
FIRST TIME, 0 VOTES

332
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:26,662
Two, three.

333
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,582
SECOND TIME, 0 VOTES

334
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:32,084
You're so popular on social media,

335
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:33,836
but not so much here.

336
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:37,173
I guess it's not meant to be.

337
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:38,382
I don't mind eating alone.

338
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:39,717
Don't be like that.

339
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:42,136
I'm so sad. I don't hear anything.

340
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,262
THEY'RE ALL WORRIED

341
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:44,763
I don't hear any footsteps.

342
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:46,599
- Are you done?
- Yes.

343
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:48,934
Then, we'll turn around now.

344
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:51,103
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

345
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:54,690
JUN-HO, ZUHA, YEON-KOUNG, KIAN

346
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:55,983
Thank you!

347
00:12:56,066 --> 00:12:57,943
What a relief!

348
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:03,073
What is this?

349
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,450
Why did you choose me?

350
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:06,952
IN-BEOM AND JUN-YEOP PICK JUN-HO

351
00:13:07,036 --> 00:13:08,329
Thank you.

352
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,831
A-JIN AND A-RIN PICK ZUHA

353
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:12,124
You won't regret it.

354
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,417
MIN-CHEOL PICKS YEON-KOUNG

355
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:14,668
I'll take good care of you.

356
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:16,879
YOUNG-GEON AND JOON-KYU PICK KIAN

357
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:19,006
It looks delicious.

358
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:21,133
You can just serve yourselves.

359
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,843
No, I'm going to do it for my friends.

360
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,303
SWOONS

361
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:25,763
What's with you?

362
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:27,181
- They picked me.
- Nice service.

363
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,182
This is my first time.

364
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:31,352
It's the first time I've ever been chosen.

365
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:33,521
Use your own chopsticks
to plate your food.

366
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,734
Where should we eat?

367
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,152
THE BOSS DOESN'T KNOW WHERE TO GO

368
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:41,862
Finding a place to eat's an ordeal too.

369
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:48,369
HE SUDDENLY CLIMBS UP THE SOFA

370
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:50,913
Yeah, I wanted to look
at this while eating.

371
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:52,957
What a great view.

372
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,625
THEY EAT BY THE WINDOW WITH GOOD VIEWS

373
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:55,543
This is nice.

374
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,503
- Where should we eat?
- Us?

375
00:13:57,586 --> 00:13:59,880
Let's make it feel like a date.

376
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,257
- Maybe here?
- Should we eat here?

377
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:02,716
IN FRONT OF HUGE TOILET PAPER ROLL

378
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:05,970
Your hand's injured,
so let's just eat down here.

379
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:07,304
IN FRONT OF TV CABINET

380
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:09,223
- Shall we eat here?
- Yes, I'd like that.

381
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:10,891
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE LIVING ROOM

382
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:13,561
- Bon appétit.
- Please enjoy.

383
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:15,646
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you for the food.

384
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,819
- It's good.
- It is? What a relief.

385
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:24,113
This is good. Zuha, it's delicious.

386
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,116
- It's good.
- It's good.

387
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:30,661
- It's good.
- It's okay?

388
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:31,829
It's delicious.

389
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:33,873
How old are you?

390
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,541
- We're the same age.
- We are?

391
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:37,251
- I was born in 2003.
- I was born in 2004.

392
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:38,168
Really?

393
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:39,712
You two look alike.

394
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:44,466
What about us looks the most similar?

395
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,926
Well…

396
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:52,474
It feels like two identical people
are looking at me.

397
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:54,602
Do you have any siblings?

398
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,312
- I'm an only child.
- Only child?

399
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,022
Let me be your sister.

400
00:14:58,105 --> 00:14:59,481
That'd be an honor.

401
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,026
I hope we become good friends here.

402
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:07,281
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

403
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:08,908
- Jun-yeop and In-beom?
- Yes.

404
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:11,493
I was really curious
about your line of work.

405
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:14,163
We had a lot of guesses earlier.
An ascetic. A rocker.

406
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,248
- A rocker?
- Someone guessed a musician.

407
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:19,418
I'm just…

408
00:15:20,252 --> 00:15:22,379
I'm just a college student.

409
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:24,214
- Just a college student?
- Yes.

410
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:25,841
What's your major?

411
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:26,842
Physical Education.

412
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:28,218
LEE IN-BEOM
MAJORING IN PE

413
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:29,219
What about you?

414
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:30,930
KIM JUN-YEOP
MAJORING IN AI

415
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:32,348
- AI?
- Yes.

416
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:33,432
Are you two

417
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:35,601
really close?

418
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:38,771
We went to the same kindergarten
when we were six.

419
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:41,482
And ever since,
we've attended the same schools.

420
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:43,567
- Really?
- We went to the same cram schools too.

421
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:45,819
- And so…
- Yeah?

422
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,738
We're supposed to enlist together too.

423
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:51,617
For real?

424
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:55,329
So we're checking out of here on March 3.

425
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:56,246
Right.

426
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,248
That's the day we enlist.

427
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:00,125
That's unbelievable.

428
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:02,211
But…

429
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:04,046
I hurt my hand last Monday.

430
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:05,255
Right.

431
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:08,592
So he's going to enter without me.

432
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:09,677
Really?

433
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:13,138
How did you hurt your hand?

434
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,306
Well…

435
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:17,309
While hitting a punching bag machine…

436
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:18,602
In an arcade?

437
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:24,858
Then, since you're enlisting soon,
did you grow out your hair on purpose?

438
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:26,527
- That's right.
- Seriously?

439
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:29,613
It must have taken years
to grow it out this long.

440
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,907
I started at the beginning of senior year.

441
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:33,701
You've grown it for two to three years?

442
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:34,827
Pretty much.

443
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,084
Do you use conditioner?

444
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:45,004
And you get hair treatments too?

445
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:50,676
What made you pick me?

446
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:52,803
Because you're an athlete too.

447
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:55,597
Then why didn't they pick me?

448
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:57,850
I'm not sure.

449
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,395
- It's different from normal rock climbing?
- Yes.

450
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:03,647
When you're rock climbing,
you use your bare hands,

451
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:05,482
- so you can feel everything.
- Right.

452
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:08,986
But we use ice axes and wear gloves.

453
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:11,196
So you need tools, not just hands.

454
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,197
Yes, we use tools.

455
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:14,783
It's ice climbing
that's been organized as a sport.

456
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:18,203
ORGANIZED AS COMPETITION ICE CLIMBING

457
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:22,499
So you're a professional?

458
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,669
It's more like a hobby for me.

459
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,087
And you came in second?

460
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,130
Yes.

461
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:29,715
Even if you sign a contract,

462
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,926
it's hard to earn enough
to make a living as a pro.

463
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:35,095
- Really?
- So you have to have another job.

464
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:36,847
I work on a mountain rescue team.

465
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,640
DAY JOB IS WITH MOUNTAIN RESCUE

466
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:40,476
Young-geon over there

467
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:42,019
is a full-time athlete.

468
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:44,313
He's currently the world champion.

469
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:47,524
So, including all the European climbers…

470
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:50,486
- The best?
- Yes, he's the best in the world.

471
00:17:50,569 --> 00:17:52,362
- The world's top-ranked climber?
- Yes.

472
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:54,406
So, you're like Yeon-koung.

473
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:55,532
In a way, yes.

474
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:57,117
Then, are you on the national team?

475
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:58,243
Yes, all three of us are.

476
00:17:58,327 --> 00:17:59,703
ICE CLIMBING NATIONAL TEAM MEMBERS

477
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,288
- Really?
- Yes.

478
00:18:01,371 --> 00:18:04,458
Then, do you get any government funding
as part of the national team?

479
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:05,751
None whatsoever.

480
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:08,670
There's a reason why
the three of us are so close.

481
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:11,173
As a niche sport,
there aren't many places for us to train.

482
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:13,759
So, we rented a greenhouse

483
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:16,178
and built a wall inside it.

484
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:17,596
We made a space for training.

485
00:18:17,679 --> 00:18:21,350
We go there in the evening
after getting off work.

486
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:23,727
So, you earn money
for competitions during the day.

487
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:24,770
Right.

488
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:26,855
Then, we train together in the evening.

489
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,441
- So, you do it because you love it.
- Yes.

490
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:31,360
- Out of passion.
- Out of passion.

491
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:32,778
- What can you do then?
- Sorry?

492
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:36,031
So as a climber,
what's the most ideal thing

493
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:39,368
you would like to see
happen in your sport?

494
00:18:39,451 --> 00:18:42,162
- First, if it becomes an Olympic sport…
- Right.

495
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,957
If it becomes an Olympic sport in 2030…

496
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:48,627
And then, our country qualifies,
and if you win an Olympic medal?

497
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:54,049
- Yes. Then, all my dreams would come true.
- That would be amazing.

498
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,342
Seriously.

499
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:58,470
Let's go back down.

500
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:00,472
Just put your trays here.

501
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:02,141
Want to play a game?

502
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:03,851
I have an idea.

503
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:04,893
How about tag?

504
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:06,019
TAG ALL OF A SUDDEN?

505
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:09,022
Tag or hide-and-seek?

506
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:10,107
AT MEETING 3 HOURS AGO

507
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,775
How about hide-and-seek?

508
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,277
Hide-and-seek.

509
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,361
YES

510
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:17,072
THAT'S THE ONE

511
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:20,075
Is there anywhere to hide?

512
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:23,871
There aren't that many places to hide.

513
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:24,955
Yeah, it's so wide open.

514
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:27,124
Let's see how creative you all are.

515
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,376
Be creative.

516
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:30,919
Right, the time limit.

517
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:33,380
It's pretty spacious,
so let's take one minute to hide.

518
00:19:33,463 --> 00:19:35,174
HIDING TIME IS 1 MINUTE

519
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,342
- Okay, let's play some hide-and-seek.
- Okay.

520
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:38,760
- Okay.
- We'll begin now.

521
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:39,887
MIN-CHEOL IS IT

522
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:41,471
There's really nowhere to hide.

523
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:45,392
JOON-KYU MOVES FAST

524
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:50,314
HE GOES FOR A PLACE OTHERS CAN'T REACH

525
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,819
BEHIND THE WEDDING DUCKS

526
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,988
Hey, I was going to hide there.

527
00:19:58,071 --> 00:19:59,865
Would you like to go in?

528
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:01,325
No, you hide there.

529
00:20:01,408 --> 00:20:02,784
I'll check how it looks for you.

530
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,161
You have to stand up.

531
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:05,829
- I should stand?
- I think you should.

532
00:20:05,913 --> 00:20:07,539
Can you tell?

533
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:08,540
Okay, that's good.

534
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:11,793
It's not bad.

535
00:20:12,502 --> 00:20:14,171
I've thought of where to hide.

536
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:16,006
YEON-KOUNG GOES UP AFTER CONCEDING HOODIE

537
00:20:22,262 --> 00:20:23,555
SHE'S TAKING OUT THE TRASH?

538
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:27,059
AND GOES IN?

539
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,603
TOO SMALL

540
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,104
Damn it.

541
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,774
WHERE WILL SHE HIDE?

542
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:35,692
I should find somewhere new.

543
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:42,950
Gosh, I can't breathe.

544
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:46,411
THE BOSS HIDES UNDER THE COMFORTERS

545
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:50,040
HIDING TIME IS OVER

546
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:50,999
Here I come.

547
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,377
THE SEARCH BEGINS

548
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,135
I think someone's here.

549
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:04,930
ZUHA'S FOUND IN 10 SECONDS

550
00:21:05,013 --> 00:21:06,431
You're it.

551
00:21:07,891 --> 00:21:09,393
I picked a bad spot.

552
00:21:10,894 --> 00:21:15,983
SEARCHING IN EARNEST

553
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:20,445
Young-geon.

554
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:25,534
No way.

555
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:27,286
He didn't climb up, did he?

556
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:32,040
Did he really climb up?

557
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:34,418
HE DID

558
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,629
Nice to see you.

559
00:21:41,049 --> 00:21:42,801
THEY'RE FOUND ONE BY ONE

560
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:44,553
This is so obvious.

561
00:21:44,636 --> 00:21:46,847
- I couldn't breathe.
- It's so hot.

562
00:21:48,473 --> 00:21:50,392
- We're so bad at this.
- I know.

563
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:53,270
Who's left?

564
00:21:53,353 --> 00:21:54,521
3 HAVEN'T BEEN FOUND YET

565
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:55,897
Where are they?

566
00:22:11,663 --> 00:22:12,622
FOUND YOU

567
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:16,126
AFTER SHE FAILED TO HIDE IN THE TRASH BIN

568
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:19,004
SHE CHANGED PLANS

569
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,052
YEON-KOUNG'S NOT HERE

570
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:29,264
TAGS

571
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:37,397
Why did you come up here?

572
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:43,320
If I had more time,
I would've hidden better.

573
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:44,404
What a shame.

574
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:48,617
SHE STILL CLEANS UP AFTER HERSELF

575
00:22:51,411 --> 00:22:52,370
Where are they?

576
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:54,748
- Where's Mr. Kian?
- Right?

577
00:22:54,831 --> 00:22:55,957
Mr. Kian.

578
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:57,751
Mr. Kian.

579
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,212
This is so stuffy.

580
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:07,886
Why hasn't he found me?

581
00:23:07,969 --> 00:23:09,346
God, I can't breathe.

582
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:11,139
Come on.

583
00:23:12,349 --> 00:23:15,769
HE WANTS TO BE FOUND SOON

584
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:22,692
He can't be here, can he?

585
00:23:26,196 --> 00:23:28,323
STICKING OUT

586
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:30,325
THE BOSS IS FOUND

587
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:34,579
He's here.

588
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:36,248
Joon-kyu, come here and lie down.

589
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:37,874
EVERYONE KNOWS WHERE HE IS NOW

590
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:41,878
Goodness.

591
00:23:42,879 --> 00:23:46,299
- Lie down properly on it.
- What are you doing?

592
00:23:47,175 --> 00:23:48,343
Hey, come on!

593
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:51,304
GROANING

594
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:53,890
Did you find me? This is so tough.

595
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:00,438
Gosh, I can't breathe.

596
00:24:02,607 --> 00:24:04,693
- Where's Jun-ho?
- He still hasn't found him yet?

597
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:06,653
- Where did he go?
- He hid so well.

598
00:24:06,736 --> 00:24:07,988
JUN-HO'S HASN'T BEEN FOUND YET

599
00:24:20,041 --> 00:24:22,294
A FOOT?

600
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:25,130
EARLIER

601
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:29,509
HE HID IN A T-SHIRT

602
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:34,389
TREMBLING

603
00:24:34,472 --> 00:24:36,433
He's here.

604
00:24:36,516 --> 00:24:38,059
Why aren't you tagging him?

605
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:40,604
It seems tough hiding there,
so I'm not tagging him.

606
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:43,607
HE CAN'T HEAR WELL

607
00:24:43,690 --> 00:24:45,400
I can do this.

608
00:24:45,483 --> 00:24:46,818
Where on earth is Jun-ho?

609
00:24:46,902 --> 00:24:48,236
Where is he? The bathroom?

610
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:50,822
SLIPPING

611
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:52,532
Where did he go?

612
00:24:53,533 --> 00:24:55,619
- Where did Jun-ho go?
- Where is he?

613
00:24:55,702 --> 00:24:56,703
Where could he be?

614
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:02,375
How long does he have to do that for?

615
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:04,586
We can't find Jun-ho.

616
00:25:04,669 --> 00:25:06,338
God. Geez.

617
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:09,132
God. Geez.

618
00:25:09,216 --> 00:25:11,092
Geez. You all knew, didn't you?

619
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:13,428
We had no idea where you were.

620
00:25:13,511 --> 00:25:16,139
- That was impressive.
- You all knew.

621
00:25:17,724 --> 00:25:18,850
I had no idea.

622
00:25:18,934 --> 00:25:21,728
Gosh, I didn't know when to come down.

623
00:25:23,438 --> 00:25:25,649
We only played one round, but we're done.

624
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:28,151
- I can't do it anymore.
- It's predictable now.

625
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:29,861
Exactly. It's over.

626
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:31,363
That was fun.

627
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:32,489
Goodness.

628
00:25:32,572 --> 00:25:34,282
Are these two just college students?

629
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:37,702
Yes, they are,
and they're entering the military soon.

630
00:25:37,786 --> 00:25:38,870
Really?

631
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:42,082
Speaking of which,
I wanted to ask Mr. Kian for a favor.

632
00:25:42,165 --> 00:25:43,333
Okay.

633
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:44,626
Certain things are required.

634
00:25:44,709 --> 00:25:45,919
Right.

635
00:25:47,754 --> 00:25:50,048
Like shaving your head.
I brought hair clippers.

636
00:25:50,131 --> 00:25:51,049
Seriously?

637
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:52,592
For real?

638
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,094
Seriously?

639
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:57,555
My enlistment's been pushed back a month,
but I can't let him do it alone.

640
00:25:57,639 --> 00:25:58,640
You're shaving it too?

641
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:00,016
SHAVING HEADS TOGETHER

642
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:02,018
- Why?
- "Why?"

643
00:26:02,602 --> 00:26:03,645
You'll regret it.

644
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:06,606
That's realistic advice.

645
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:07,899
For your friend?

646
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:10,277
Yes. I was supposed to do it anyway.

647
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:15,115
Think it over again,
and if you still want to shave it then…

648
00:26:15,198 --> 00:26:17,325
Well, it's not my hair,
so you can if you want.

649
00:26:17,993 --> 00:26:19,411
But you might regret it.

650
00:26:19,494 --> 00:26:20,787
I won't.

651
00:26:21,621 --> 00:26:23,123
A loyal friend.

652
00:26:23,206 --> 00:26:24,916
KIAN'S B&B

653
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,376
Have a drink.

654
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:27,460
10:00 P.M.

655
00:26:28,962 --> 00:26:30,630
LIGHTING PROVIDED TO SET THE MOOD

656
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:32,465
This is so romantic.

657
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:36,720
- This is perfect.
- Tonight's mood is so nice.

658
00:26:36,803 --> 00:26:38,847
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

659
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:41,599
Thank you. Welcome.

660
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:43,601
Did you sketch everything this time too?

661
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:44,853
Yes.

662
00:26:46,146 --> 00:26:48,148
- It's like <i>Gulliver's Travels.</i>
- Right?

663
00:26:48,231 --> 00:26:50,025
- It's like the theme.
- And there's me.

664
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:52,569
NODDING

665
00:26:52,652 --> 00:26:54,154
I've never met
a woman taller than me.

666
00:26:54,237 --> 00:26:56,323
"A woman taller than me."

667
00:26:56,406 --> 00:26:58,074
- How tall are you?
- I'm 186 cm.

668
00:26:58,158 --> 00:27:00,035
You're 186 cm? That's pretty short.

669
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:01,745
- "Pretty short"!
- "Short"!

670
00:27:01,828 --> 00:27:03,747
In volleyball,
a lot of people are your height.

671
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,166
That's a cute height.

672
00:27:07,417 --> 00:27:08,626
I'll call you my big sis.

673
00:27:09,669 --> 00:27:11,588
Do I look gloomy to you, by any chance?

674
00:27:11,671 --> 00:27:13,214
OUT OF THE BLUE?

675
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,716
- You look cheerful.
- The thing is…

676
00:27:14,799 --> 00:27:17,677
One of the guests made… a claim?

677
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:18,720
- A complaint?
- Yes.

678
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:21,181
"Mr. Kian, you look so dark."

679
00:27:21,264 --> 00:27:23,892
So when you arrived earlier,
I tried really hard.

680
00:27:23,975 --> 00:27:25,185
- Really?
- Yes.

681
00:27:25,268 --> 00:27:27,020
But you welcomed us so warmly.

682
00:27:27,103 --> 00:27:29,814
To be honest, you're celebrities to us,

683
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:32,317
so there was a wall,
but I feel like that came down.

684
00:27:32,942 --> 00:27:34,444
That's what we wanted.

685
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:36,613
You came all the way here,
so you should have fun.

686
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:38,823
And you're entering the military soon.

687
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:40,158
Right.

688
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:41,868
- You're going there right away?
- Yes.

689
00:27:41,951 --> 00:27:43,661
Straight to our military unit.

690
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:45,246
- Really?
- What?

691
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,706
Right after checking out?

692
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:48,833
Straight to boot camp?
What about your parents?

693
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:51,002
I'm going to meet them there.

694
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:53,046
- That's insane.
- Really?

695
00:27:53,129 --> 00:27:54,089
My goodness.

696
00:27:54,172 --> 00:27:56,424
Did you say goodbye
to your friends already?

697
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:57,717
Yes, I did.

698
00:28:00,303 --> 00:28:02,138
I was supposed to join him.

699
00:28:03,848 --> 00:28:05,475
Gosh, you're going into the military?

700
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:09,270
Straight to the military from here?

701
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:15,276
FEELING SAD FOR SOME REASON

702
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:22,367
Hey, you guys come here.
Let's drink over here.

703
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:24,077
Where should we drink?

704
00:28:24,619 --> 00:28:26,079
Could we borrow this room?

705
00:28:26,162 --> 00:28:27,747
- Yes.
- Yes, of course.

706
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:29,040
Thank you.

707
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:32,544
Don't be so formal. Why are you kneeling?

708
00:28:34,045 --> 00:28:35,463
- In-beom?
- Yes.

709
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:37,507
You two went to the same schools.

710
00:28:37,590 --> 00:28:39,092
From kindergarten to high school.

711
00:28:39,175 --> 00:28:41,094
- Including kindergarten too?
- Yes.

712
00:28:41,177 --> 00:28:42,595
I've told him since middle school.

713
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:45,306
"We have to enlist
in the military together."

714
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:47,434
- So it was your idea.
- Yes.

715
00:28:48,017 --> 00:28:49,811
But that's such a one-sided love.

716
00:28:50,645 --> 00:28:52,397
Well, he does like me a lot.

717
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,940
And he's your best friend too?

718
00:28:54,023 --> 00:28:54,941
Yes, he is.

719
00:28:55,024 --> 00:28:57,193
- Is he the only one who thinks this?
- Not at all.

720
00:28:57,277 --> 00:28:59,195
I also had such a friend
in elementary school.

721
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,113
Really?

722
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:03,616
You know, boys always have to decide
who their number one friend is.

723
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:05,827
- You know what I mean?
- I do.

724
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:07,746
He was my best friend back then.

725
00:29:07,829 --> 00:29:10,582
- My favorite friend in the whole world.
- Right.

726
00:29:10,665 --> 00:29:13,042
I had such a friend.
His name was Sang-gyeom.

727
00:29:13,626 --> 00:29:15,712
It was always,
"My best friend, Sang-gyeom."

728
00:29:15,795 --> 00:29:18,798
"Let's go to this middle school.
Let's go to high school together."

729
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:21,593
"Let's enter the military together."
I'd always say that.

730
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:22,510
EMPATHIZING

731
00:29:22,594 --> 00:29:23,845
Then, you know how I feel.

732
00:29:23,928 --> 00:29:25,555
Did you ever watch the show <i>High Kick?</i>

733
00:29:25,638 --> 00:29:28,725
Kim Bum would always go over
to the main character's house.

734
00:29:28,808 --> 00:29:30,018
I was the same way.

735
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:32,729
His mother would ask,
"Aren't you going to go home?"

736
00:29:32,812 --> 00:29:34,522
And I'd say, "But I like it here."

737
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:36,357
- I liked hanging out with my friend.
- Right.

738
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:38,151
I go over to his house often too.

739
00:29:38,234 --> 00:29:41,613
Then, he made another close friend later.

740
00:29:41,696 --> 00:29:42,572
I was so jealous.

741
00:29:43,656 --> 00:29:46,868
"He left me out
and became friends with someone else?"

742
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:48,286
I know how that feels.

743
00:29:48,369 --> 00:29:51,706
When we first entered high school,

744
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:54,834
he'd try to become friends
with his new classmates.

745
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:57,337
And he'd have sleepovers at his house.

746
00:29:58,129 --> 00:30:00,215
- And I was so hurt in middle school.
- Right.

747
00:30:00,715 --> 00:30:04,552
He was so important to me
that I didn't make any other friends…

748
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:07,972
"You're my only friend,
but you're having fun with other kids?"

749
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:11,184
Right. Without him,
I'd have to just go home.

750
00:30:11,267 --> 00:30:13,311
Yeah, and you have to
join the military together.

751
00:30:13,394 --> 00:30:16,523
But you can't right now,
so it must be really frustrating for you.

752
00:30:16,606 --> 00:30:17,857
It is.

753
00:30:17,941 --> 00:30:20,735
You'll have to go through a lot
in the military anyway.

754
00:30:20,819 --> 00:30:23,112
If you entered together,
that would've been a dream.

755
00:30:23,696 --> 00:30:25,114
But your dream's been broken.

756
00:30:25,198 --> 00:30:27,283
I was the same.

757
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:30,161
It was my dream to attend
the same high school as him.

758
00:30:31,204 --> 00:30:34,707
But when it didn't happen,
it drove me crazy.

759
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:36,835
- And it's happening to you.
- Right.

760
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:40,004
It's like watching my young self.

761
00:30:41,339 --> 00:30:42,674
Seriously?

762
00:30:46,511 --> 00:30:49,430
All right.
Let's have a drink again tomorrow.

763
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:51,766
And we'll shave your hair.
What time is it?

764
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,268
It's 12:57 a.m. Almost 1:00 a.m.

765
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:55,353
- Did you finish talking?
- Yes.

766
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:59,858
Our 21-year-old friends…

767
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:02,402
They have a true friendship.

768
00:31:02,485 --> 00:31:03,820
Yes, since kindergarten.

769
00:31:03,903 --> 00:31:06,322
So they were supposed to enlist together,

770
00:31:06,406 --> 00:31:07,824
but he can't with his hurt hand.

771
00:31:08,408 --> 00:31:09,909
Isn't this such a beautiful story?

772
00:31:09,993 --> 00:31:11,828
Just have a drink,
and stop talking nonsense.

773
00:31:11,911 --> 00:31:13,705
JUMPS UP AGAIN

774
00:31:13,788 --> 00:31:16,124
As soon as In-beom checks out later on…

775
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:17,292
REPEATING HIMSELF

776
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:19,711
…he's going straight to the military.

777
00:31:19,794 --> 00:31:21,546
How many times are you going to say that?

778
00:31:21,629 --> 00:31:24,549
This is something
I need to say over and over again.

779
00:31:25,967 --> 00:31:27,343
We can't forget it.

780
00:31:27,427 --> 00:31:29,387
- We didn't forget.
- I will…

781
00:31:29,470 --> 00:31:31,973
I'll tell you this again tomorrow,

782
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:33,182
so prepare yourselves.

783
00:31:36,227 --> 00:31:38,521
WHILE THEY TALK AND LAUGH

784
00:31:41,274 --> 00:31:45,153
IT STARTS TO QUIETLY SNOW

785
00:31:45,236 --> 00:31:47,113
It's snowing.

786
00:31:47,906 --> 00:31:50,116
- It's snowing hard.
- It's snowing right now.

787
00:31:50,199 --> 00:31:51,576
It's snowing, Boss.

788
00:31:51,659 --> 00:31:52,744
It is.

789
00:31:53,661 --> 00:31:56,164
It hadn't snowed until now.

790
00:31:56,247 --> 00:31:58,374
- Let's have a snowball fight tomorrow.
- Yes.

791
00:31:58,458 --> 00:32:00,251
And we should make a snowman.

792
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:01,669
Yes, a snowman.

793
00:32:02,545 --> 00:32:03,922
But it's snowing a lot.

794
00:32:04,005 --> 00:32:06,341
A BIT INTENSE

795
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:08,468
It's not good if we can't go out tomorrow.

796
00:32:08,551 --> 00:32:09,844
Right, that can't happen.

797
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:12,388
Let's just put this to the side.

798
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:13,514
THEY WRAP UP

799
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:16,893
AND GO TO THEIR RESPECTIVE BEDS

800
00:32:19,395 --> 00:32:20,688
Min-cheol might snore a lot.

801
00:32:20,772 --> 00:32:21,940
MIN-CHEOL, YOUNG-GEON: FRIDGE

802
00:32:22,023 --> 00:32:23,107
We better sleep now.

803
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:24,192
A-JIN, A-RIN: TV CABINET

804
00:32:24,275 --> 00:32:26,861
JUN-YEOP, IN-BEOM, JOON-KYU: LIVING ROOM

805
00:32:27,445 --> 00:32:29,155
- Sleep tight, Boss.
- Good night.

806
00:32:29,238 --> 00:32:30,073
Good night.

807
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:31,032
HANGERS

808
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:33,952
I mean, that's some pretty heavy snowfall.

809
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:35,286
THE SNOW SUDDENLY GETS HEAVIER

810
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:37,205
There was a heavy-snow alert.

811
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:39,749
HEAVY SNOW EXPECTED OVERNIGHT IN GANGWON

812
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:41,542
What if we can't open the door tomorrow?

813
00:32:42,251 --> 00:32:47,256
THE SNOW SLOWLY FALLS EVEN HARDER

814
00:32:54,764 --> 00:32:59,519
DAY 7

815
00:32:59,602 --> 00:33:01,813
KIAN'S B&B

816
00:33:04,148 --> 00:33:06,442
IT'S BEEN SNOWING FOR 7 HOURS

817
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:09,696
8:00 A.M.

818
00:33:09,779 --> 00:33:11,739
How many times have you used the sauna?

819
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:14,575
The sauna? A lot of times.

820
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:16,285
Almost every day.

821
00:33:16,369 --> 00:33:17,704
People used it if they wanted to.

822
00:33:17,787 --> 00:33:19,497
ZUHA, A-JIN, AND A-RIN HAVE A MORNING CHAT

823
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:22,542
Let's pack the equipment.

824
00:33:22,625 --> 00:33:24,043
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

825
00:33:24,127 --> 00:33:25,086
Did you sleep well?

826
00:33:25,169 --> 00:33:26,796
How long does it take to get there?

827
00:33:26,879 --> 00:33:27,797
About two hours.

828
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:28,798
- Two hours?
- Yes.

829
00:33:28,881 --> 00:33:30,591
Then, it's a four-hour round trip?

830
00:33:31,175 --> 00:33:33,845
If we don't go climb the ice walls now…

831
00:33:33,928 --> 00:33:35,888
- Now's the only time?
- Exactly.

832
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:39,726
Can I take a look, Min-cheol?

833
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:44,105
So you wear gloves
and stick these into the ice to climb up?

834
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:45,148
Yes, that's for speed.

835
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:46,774
- For speed climbing?
- Yes.

836
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:49,110
Gosh, it's pretty big.

837
00:33:49,819 --> 00:33:51,320
The tools are all…

838
00:33:51,404 --> 00:33:53,781
Gosh, this is no joke.

839
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:55,408
I wish we had these here.

840
00:33:55,491 --> 00:33:56,993
It's so hard to climb that.

841
00:33:57,493 --> 00:33:58,911
Don't your feet hurt?

842
00:33:58,995 --> 00:34:00,580
Give it a try.

843
00:34:00,663 --> 00:34:02,373
I guess you do it like this.

844
00:34:02,457 --> 00:34:03,958
- Right?
- That's right.

845
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:05,376
- Like this?
- Yes.

846
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:06,502
That's it.

847
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:07,754
- Like this?
- Yes.

848
00:34:07,837 --> 00:34:09,589
This is better.

849
00:34:09,672 --> 00:34:10,965
INTRIGUED

850
00:34:13,926 --> 00:34:15,887
YEON-KOUNG SLEPT IN

851
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:19,682
AFTER ALSO SLEEPING IN, THE BOSS GETS UP

852
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:26,647
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes.

853
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:27,648
Yes.

854
00:34:31,819 --> 00:34:32,987
Boss is here.

855
00:34:33,529 --> 00:34:35,740
You look clean. You washed up.

856
00:34:35,823 --> 00:34:37,325
Yes, I took a shower.

857
00:34:37,408 --> 00:34:38,910
SATISFIED

858
00:34:38,993 --> 00:34:41,204
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes, very well.

859
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:42,538
Did you sleep well, Boss?

860
00:34:43,289 --> 00:34:45,374
I feel like my body's broken.

861
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:46,667
I feel so worn out.

862
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:49,462
- It's a battle of stamina.
- This is a workout.

863
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:52,799
We'll open that later in the evening.

864
00:34:52,882 --> 00:34:54,759
- The jacuzzi.
- Tonight? That's good.

865
00:34:54,842 --> 00:34:56,219
Everyone, have a safe trip.

866
00:34:56,302 --> 00:34:58,137
Will they be okay with the snow?

867
00:34:58,221 --> 00:34:59,931
I don't think it'll stop soon.

868
00:35:00,014 --> 00:35:01,390
The snow is no joke outside.

869
00:35:01,974 --> 00:35:03,893
THE PATH IS COVERED IN SNOW

870
00:35:03,976 --> 00:35:05,978
SO ARE THE GUESTS' CARS

871
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:09,565
THEY DECIDE TO HEAD OUT

872
00:35:11,150 --> 00:35:13,277
Where are you going, Jun-ho?

873
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,947
I'll go clear the snow off their car

874
00:35:16,030 --> 00:35:17,782
and apply some liquid tire chain.

875
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:19,909
I'll be back.

876
00:35:21,035 --> 00:35:23,079
HE GOES TO STORAGE
TO GET SNOW REMOVAL TOOLS

877
00:35:24,747 --> 00:35:26,082
This should do.

878
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:29,293
This is no joke.

879
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:33,214
It snowed so much.

880
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:34,924
It's unbelievable.

881
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:37,760
I can't believe how the scenery
just changed like this.

882
00:35:38,719 --> 00:35:39,762
See you later.

883
00:35:39,846 --> 00:35:41,889
- See you.
- See you.

884
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:44,267
- See you.
- How many days left until the military?

885
00:35:44,350 --> 00:35:45,893
I'm going tomorrow.

886
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,520
You're entering tomorrow?

887
00:35:47,603 --> 00:35:48,563
Yes.

888
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:51,190
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

889
00:35:53,860 --> 00:35:55,236
- I'll get going.
- Okay.

890
00:35:55,319 --> 00:35:57,530
- You're not cold, Jun-yeop?
- No.

891
00:35:57,613 --> 00:35:58,739
I'm okay now, so…

892
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:01,200
But it'll get cold later. Put mine on.

893
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:04,203
You're going to wear that
in Daegwallyeong in February?

894
00:36:04,787 --> 00:36:05,788
Thank you.

895
00:36:07,373 --> 00:36:09,292
- We'll get going.
- See you.

896
00:36:09,792 --> 00:36:11,586
WARM IN THE BOSS'S JACKET AS HE HEADS OUT

897
00:36:11,669 --> 00:36:13,379
It really wasn't me.

898
00:36:13,462 --> 00:36:14,755
Which one's your car?

899
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:16,048
This one.

900
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:19,927
HE REMOVES SNOW FROM THE GUEST'S CARS

901
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:24,265
This is no joke.

902
00:36:26,475 --> 00:36:28,686
It should be okay
if you turn the wipers on.

903
00:36:29,270 --> 00:36:30,313
A-JIN AND A-RIN'S CAR TOO

904
00:36:30,396 --> 00:36:31,355
Your hand must be cold.

905
00:36:35,902 --> 00:36:36,986
Thank you.

906
00:36:37,069 --> 00:36:38,154
- Have a safe trip.
- We will.

907
00:36:38,237 --> 00:36:39,530
WHILE JUN-HO TENDS TO THE GUESTS

908
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:44,202
We need to shovel the snow.

909
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:46,829
What's going on?

910
00:36:47,413 --> 00:36:49,040
What happened overnight?

911
00:36:49,123 --> 00:36:50,499
I should put on gloves.

912
00:36:50,583 --> 00:36:52,877
TODAY'S ADDITIONAL TASK
SNOW REMOVAL

913
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:55,338
We can't even sweep
this lumpy snow though.

914
00:36:57,298 --> 00:37:00,218
Still, clearing snow is our job.

915
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:01,636
My gosh.

916
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:04,472
ZUHA ALSO STARTS

917
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:06,599
I'll sweep some away first,
and you push it aside.

918
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:07,934
Okay.

919
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,773
JUST FOLLOW ME

920
00:37:15,816 --> 00:37:17,735
LIGHT BRUSHING

921
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:20,821
It'll take all day if you do it like that.

922
00:37:21,781 --> 00:37:22,698
Harder.

923
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:24,533
Sweep back and forth like this.

924
00:37:26,494 --> 00:37:27,828
HARDER?

925
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:29,205
Harder.

926
00:37:29,288 --> 00:37:31,207
LIGHTLY

927
00:37:32,667 --> 00:37:34,085
PAUSING

928
00:37:34,168 --> 00:37:35,670
Zuha, you're not working hard today.

929
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:38,506
I was watching how you did it.

930
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:39,715
You go to the front.

931
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:41,425
You're sweeping what I already swept.

932
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:43,970
Busted.

933
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:46,764
Longer strokes. All the way.

934
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,475
And go forward.

935
00:37:49,558 --> 00:37:50,601
That's it.

936
00:37:51,477 --> 00:37:52,478
Good.

937
00:37:53,479 --> 00:37:54,689
You're doing well.

938
00:37:58,192 --> 00:37:59,193
Go.

939
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:01,070
- We have to sweep the whole path.
- All of it?

940
00:38:01,153 --> 00:38:03,239
- The whole path.
- Seriously?

941
00:38:03,322 --> 00:38:06,117
THEY HAVE TO SWEEP THE WHOLE PATH

942
00:38:06,742 --> 00:38:09,078
We can't have them
slip on their way back.

943
00:38:09,161 --> 00:38:10,579
- Understand?
- Yes.

944
00:38:11,455 --> 00:38:13,666
Where did Boss go?

945
00:38:13,749 --> 00:38:14,583
THE BOSS IS…

946
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:16,168
This is hopeless.

947
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:17,753
SHOVELING

948
00:38:18,796 --> 00:38:21,090
UNCOVERS MAT THAT HAD VANISHED

949
00:38:25,886 --> 00:38:27,513
CLEARING PATH, CLEARING ENTRANCE

950
00:38:29,015 --> 00:38:31,434
Damn it. Is it frozen? What's with this?

951
00:38:31,934 --> 00:38:33,561
THE MAT IS SAVED

952
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:35,521
Great job.

953
00:38:36,605 --> 00:38:37,440
You're doing great.

954
00:38:37,523 --> 00:38:38,941
- Hurry and join us.
- Okay.

955
00:38:40,818 --> 00:38:42,236
It must've been tough.

956
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:43,612
RETURNS AFTER SEEING GUESTS OFF

957
00:38:44,196 --> 00:38:45,489
I should go and clear that path.

958
00:38:46,574 --> 00:38:48,743
JUN-HO CLEARS ANOTHER PATH

959
00:38:50,745 --> 00:38:51,996
FROZEN SOLID

960
00:38:58,836 --> 00:39:01,172
THE BOSS STARTS CLEARING
ONE END OF THE PATH

961
00:39:06,010 --> 00:39:07,136
I'm so tired.

962
00:39:08,596 --> 00:39:09,972
Gosh, this is…

963
00:39:10,056 --> 00:39:10,890
DIGGING

964
00:39:10,973 --> 00:39:12,767
It won't break loose.

965
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:16,604
LOOKING AROUND

966
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:18,981
It keeps snowing.

967
00:39:19,815 --> 00:39:21,942
SNOWING HEAVILY

968
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:25,905
PILING UP AGAIN

969
00:39:25,988 --> 00:39:27,990
Hey, this is endless.

970
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:29,617
It's endless.

971
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:31,369
It keeps snowing.

972
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:32,370
Yeon-koung!

973
00:39:34,538 --> 00:39:36,165
- Stop!
- Stop?

974
00:39:36,248 --> 00:39:37,917
I should go all the way.

975
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,251
It keeps snowing.

976
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:42,213
Still, it's better to clear it,
so their feet won't sink in.

977
00:39:42,296 --> 00:39:43,631
I'll go all the way to the end.

978
00:39:43,714 --> 00:39:44,965
- All the way?
- Yes.

979
00:39:45,549 --> 00:39:47,218
We might as well do it now.

980
00:39:47,301 --> 00:39:48,135
All right.

981
00:39:48,219 --> 00:39:50,304
When they come back later,
it won't be slippery.

982
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:54,266
WE HAVE TO DO THIS THEN

983
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:03,025
We should clear as much as we can.

984
00:40:04,235 --> 00:40:06,737
Geez, Boss. This is too tough.

985
00:40:07,988 --> 00:40:10,074
Hang in there. We're almost done.

986
00:40:10,658 --> 00:40:11,742
My hands are so cold.

987
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,828
You got the hang of it now. Yes, Zuha.

988
00:40:13,911 --> 00:40:15,913
Yes, push and sweep. There you go!

989
00:40:16,622 --> 00:40:19,708
Good. You got much better, Zuha.

990
00:40:24,839 --> 00:40:27,007
THE PATH IS ALL CLEARED

991
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:28,384
All the way.

992
00:40:28,467 --> 00:40:29,677
ZUHA WORKS HARD UNTIL THE END

993
00:40:30,845 --> 00:40:31,720
Take a seat.

994
00:40:33,222 --> 00:40:34,890
GROANING

995
00:40:34,974 --> 00:40:36,851
It looks so cool. Look over there.

996
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:42,773
- Nice, right?
- Yes.

997
00:40:46,068 --> 00:40:47,903
As the snow falls over you,

998
00:40:47,987 --> 00:40:50,281
you don't get to experience
something like this often.

999
00:40:50,364 --> 00:40:52,450
Yes, you're right.

1000
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:53,659
It's really rare.

1001
00:40:54,243 --> 00:40:55,661
The way I see it,

1002
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:58,747
it'll pile up again.

1003
00:40:58,831 --> 00:41:00,583
Don't say that.

1004
00:41:00,666 --> 00:41:02,293
- Still, it's better than before.
- It is.

1005
00:41:02,376 --> 00:41:04,211
- It's flat now.
- Right.

1006
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:06,088
Kian's B&B is all about stamina.

1007
00:41:06,172 --> 00:41:08,966
Most people wouldn't be able to handle it.

1008
00:41:09,049 --> 00:41:11,010
They would fall sick.

1009
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:12,344
Let's go.

1010
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:14,013
- We're going?
- We should go back.

1011
00:41:14,096 --> 00:41:15,014
- Now?
- Let's go.

1012
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:16,599
Let's sweep as we go.

1013
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:23,230
Yeon-koung, that's enough.

1014
00:41:24,940 --> 00:41:27,234
Let's go sledding.

1015
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:29,320
- I want to ride.
- I'll bring them over.

1016
00:41:29,403 --> 00:41:30,488
Here they are.

1017
00:41:32,948 --> 00:41:35,284
A SACK FOR THE BOSS
AND SLEDS FOR EMPLOYEES

1018
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:37,661
GRINNING WIDELY

1019
00:41:38,287 --> 00:41:39,914
Isn't this course too advanced?

1020
00:41:39,997 --> 00:41:41,999
STEEPER THAN EXPECTED

1021
00:41:42,082 --> 00:41:43,083
I should get a sled too.

1022
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:44,376
HE GOES TO GET A SLED TOO

1023
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:46,420
You're really going?

1024
00:41:46,504 --> 00:41:48,714
- This is a piece of cake.
- Yeah.

1025
00:41:49,298 --> 00:41:50,508
I'll go first.

1026
00:41:50,591 --> 00:41:52,760
JUN-HO GOES FIRST

1027
00:41:52,843 --> 00:41:53,719
Here I go!

1028
00:42:01,268 --> 00:42:02,353
How is it?

1029
00:42:02,436 --> 00:42:03,896
STAGGERS

1030
00:42:04,647 --> 00:42:05,564
Is it fun?

1031
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:07,358
- It is fun.
- Really?

1032
00:42:07,942 --> 00:42:09,735
It's so fast. Be careful here.

1033
00:42:09,818 --> 00:42:11,070
A BIT NERVOUS

1034
00:42:11,153 --> 00:42:13,072
- Are you going?
- Of course.

1035
00:42:13,155 --> 00:42:14,073
WAIT FOR ME

1036
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:15,449
- Is it fun?
- He says it is.

1037
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:17,368
Come on down. I'll catch you.

1038
00:42:30,297 --> 00:42:31,840
How far are you going?

1039
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:34,343
It's no joke! Hey, it's no joke.

1040
00:42:34,426 --> 00:42:36,679
- I underestimated it, Jun-ho.
- You can get off.

1041
00:42:36,762 --> 00:42:38,055
It's no joke!

1042
00:42:38,138 --> 00:42:39,265
Be careful.

1043
00:42:39,765 --> 00:42:41,225
It's faster than you think.

1044
00:42:43,102 --> 00:42:45,980
GOES EVEN FASTER

1045
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:49,108
ZUHA IS FLYING

1046
00:42:55,030 --> 00:42:58,242
- You were flying since you're light.
- Right, you were so fast.

1047
00:42:59,952 --> 00:43:01,245
Hey, don't catch me.

1048
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:02,329
Don't catch you?

1049
00:43:02,413 --> 00:43:03,872
No. Here I go!

1050
00:43:06,625 --> 00:43:08,377
AIRBORNE

1051
00:43:08,460 --> 00:43:10,087
HIGH SPEED

1052
00:43:10,170 --> 00:43:12,089
- He's so fast.
- That's it.

1053
00:43:16,176 --> 00:43:17,469
Move out of the way!

1054
00:43:18,512 --> 00:43:19,597
Move out of the way.

1055
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:22,182
Move out of the way!

1056
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:24,977
Hey, this is fun!

1057
00:43:25,060 --> 00:43:26,061
SO THRILLING

1058
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:27,896
LET'S DO IT AGAIN!

1059
00:43:27,980 --> 00:43:30,107
I'm pretty sure poop
is everywhere around here.

1060
00:43:30,190 --> 00:43:31,400
You're right.

1061
00:43:34,903 --> 00:43:36,739
- He's fast.
- He's so fast.

1062
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:42,953
This is no joke. Come on!

1063
00:44:00,971 --> 00:44:02,222
I bumped into that.

1064
00:44:02,306 --> 00:44:03,807
I think you can't pull so hard.

1065
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:06,518
- Don't pull? Okay.
- If you do, you'll stop.

1066
00:44:06,602 --> 00:44:08,312
TRYING AGAIN

1067
00:44:08,979 --> 00:44:10,356
Okay, it's this feeling!

1068
00:44:11,190 --> 00:44:12,608
I like this feeling.

1069
00:44:13,484 --> 00:44:15,319
A SLED FULL OF HAPPINESS

1070
00:44:15,903 --> 00:44:18,030
This is removing the snow automatically.

1071
00:44:18,781 --> 00:44:19,990
I can't see anything.

1072
00:44:20,074 --> 00:44:21,367
THEY ALL LOOK LIKE A MESS

1073
00:44:23,160 --> 00:44:24,578
Want to make a snowman?

1074
00:44:24,662 --> 00:44:26,497
- A snowman?
- Yeah, the snow sticks so well.

1075
00:44:26,580 --> 00:44:28,624
THE SNOWMAN WAS A LIE

1076
00:44:30,542 --> 00:44:31,752
The snow hurts a bit.

1077
00:44:31,835 --> 00:44:33,629
THEY MOVE INTO BATTLE FORMATION

1078
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:35,255
Jun-ho, thanks for your work.

1079
00:44:36,340 --> 00:44:37,800
A SNOWBALL OF LOVE?

1080
00:44:37,883 --> 00:44:39,760
- Yeon-koung.
- What?

1081
00:44:39,843 --> 00:44:41,011
DELIVERS A SNOWBALL OF LOVE

1082
00:44:41,095 --> 00:44:42,304
I love you!

1083
00:44:43,138 --> 00:44:44,848
BLOCKS THE LOVE

1084
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:46,308
What on earth?

1085
00:44:46,392 --> 00:44:48,018
RIGHT, SHE WAS A VOLLEYBALL PLAYER

1086
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:51,063
Hey, let's count to three
and throw it at a person of your choice.

1087
00:44:51,146 --> 00:44:52,898
You know what I mean?

1088
00:44:55,859 --> 00:44:57,194
You know what I mean, right?

1089
00:44:57,277 --> 00:44:58,362
ONLY ONE WHO DOESN'T KNOW

1090
00:44:58,445 --> 00:45:00,656
- Okay. One…
- Two…

1091
00:45:00,739 --> 00:45:01,782
Three!

1092
00:45:08,247 --> 00:45:10,541
FIGHTING BACK

1093
00:45:11,458 --> 00:45:12,876
DEADLOCKED

1094
00:45:13,669 --> 00:45:14,753
Hey!

1095
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:17,506
You fooled me into coming here. Come here!

1096
00:45:22,845 --> 00:45:24,221
RUNNING AWAY

1097
00:45:24,304 --> 00:45:25,639
She and I wrestled a bit,

1098
00:45:25,722 --> 00:45:27,766
but she didn't punch me or anything.

1099
00:45:27,850 --> 00:45:29,184
She's kind-hearted.

1100
00:45:29,268 --> 00:45:31,395
KIND-HEARTED FRIEND

1101
00:45:32,062 --> 00:45:34,148
I'm so exhausted.

1102
00:45:34,857 --> 00:45:35,983
This is insane.

1103
00:45:36,066 --> 00:45:37,484
Gosh, that was so damn funny.

1104
00:45:38,068 --> 00:45:39,695
- I'm hungry now.
- What?

1105
00:45:39,778 --> 00:45:41,321
- We should go eat.
- Right.

1106
00:45:41,405 --> 00:45:42,781
SO BUSY PLAYING THEY FORGOT TO EAT

1107
00:45:42,865 --> 00:45:43,866
Is there anything to eat?

1108
00:45:43,949 --> 00:45:45,367
Let's go in and see.

1109
00:45:46,076 --> 00:45:48,579
Maybe we shouldn't have used up
our energy before cleaning.

1110
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:54,543
I should wash up.

1111
00:45:54,626 --> 00:45:56,336
I am so spent.

1112
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:58,422
Gosh, I feel so cold.

1113
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,507
- Are you cold?
- I am.

1114
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:06,638
This is so nice.

1115
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:09,141
WARM

1116
00:46:09,224 --> 00:46:10,392
- Yeon-koung.
- Yes?

1117
00:46:10,476 --> 00:46:14,021
You know, if more guests come,

1118
00:46:14,104 --> 00:46:15,939
could you give your room to them?

1119
00:46:16,023 --> 00:46:18,108
Sure. Let's move out of our rooms.

1120
00:46:18,192 --> 00:46:19,276
Okay.

1121
00:46:19,359 --> 00:46:21,278
- Let's just sleep here.
- Okay.

1122
00:46:21,361 --> 00:46:23,614
- Hey, warm yourself up.
- Yeah, I should.

1123
00:46:25,449 --> 00:46:27,075
I feel sleepy now.

1124
00:46:27,659 --> 00:46:29,077
SLEEPY

1125
00:46:30,412 --> 00:46:31,371
What do we eat?

1126
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:33,707
Let's order in today.

1127
00:46:33,790 --> 00:46:35,334
Yeah, let's order something.

1128
00:46:35,417 --> 00:46:37,002
LOOKING AT A DELIVERY APP

1129
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:38,837
- Order what you want to eat.
- Yeah.

1130
00:46:38,921 --> 00:46:40,464
SHE CHOOSES KOREAN FOOD

1131
00:46:40,547 --> 00:46:41,965
I'll have pork backbone soup.

1132
00:46:42,049 --> 00:46:44,510
This is what Zuha chose? Hangover soup?

1133
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:46,011
SO HAPPY CHOOSING WHAT TO EAT

1134
00:46:46,094 --> 00:46:48,555
Hey. I'm sorry to say this, but…

1135
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:51,642
I have bad news.

1136
00:46:51,725 --> 00:46:54,978
It says, "Due to inclement weather
caused by snow, delivery is unavailable."

1137
00:46:55,062 --> 00:46:55,938
A DEVASTATING

1138
00:46:56,021 --> 00:46:57,147
SURPRISE

1139
00:46:59,525 --> 00:47:01,193
EVEN THE DOOR FLIES OPEN

1140
00:47:01,276 --> 00:47:03,070
We said
we should've ordered in yesterday!

1141
00:47:03,153 --> 00:47:04,446
Let us get delivery.

1142
00:47:06,281 --> 00:47:07,908
We told you yesterday.

1143
00:47:07,991 --> 00:47:09,826
We told you yesterday!

1144
00:47:09,910 --> 00:47:12,371
I told you we should order in yesterday!

1145
00:47:12,955 --> 00:47:14,039
Everyone.

1146
00:47:14,122 --> 00:47:17,209
Embracing the unpredictable
is the joy of life.

1147
00:47:17,292 --> 00:47:18,710
<i>Ramyeon</i> again?

1148
00:47:20,087 --> 00:47:21,296
One, two, three.

1149
00:47:23,966 --> 00:47:26,718
I'll cook something up quickly.
Leave it to me.

1150
00:47:29,179 --> 00:47:30,055
WASHES RICE

1151
00:47:30,639 --> 00:47:32,975
PUTS IN CHOPPED VEGETABLES

1152
00:47:33,058 --> 00:47:34,726
GOCHUJANG

1153
00:47:35,394 --> 00:47:36,687
SESAME OIL

1154
00:47:38,355 --> 00:47:40,983
A LOT OF CHEESE

1155
00:47:41,858 --> 00:47:43,860
RAMYEON SOUP POWDER FOR EXTRA FLAVOR

1156
00:47:45,320 --> 00:47:47,155
ADDS PROTEIN TOO

1157
00:47:51,618 --> 00:47:52,828
- Is it a stew?
- Yeah.

1158
00:47:52,911 --> 00:47:54,913
PRESUMABLY SOME KIND OF THICK STEW

1159
00:47:56,873 --> 00:47:58,584
NATURALLY SITS
IN FRONT OF SINK WITH DISHES

1160
00:47:58,667 --> 00:47:59,501
We didn't do them,

1161
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:01,336
- so there's a lot from yesterday.
- Right.

1162
00:48:04,089 --> 00:48:06,216
Geez, how many times have we washed these?

1163
00:48:06,300 --> 00:48:08,176
- Gosh, my back.
- Goodness.

1164
00:48:08,260 --> 00:48:09,761
Gosh, my back!

1165
00:48:09,845 --> 00:48:11,221
Goodness!

1166
00:48:11,305 --> 00:48:13,348
I feel like we're always
cleaning this darn house.

1167
00:48:13,432 --> 00:48:14,474
CLEANING DOWNSTAIRS

1168
00:48:14,558 --> 00:48:15,976
Our chores keep piling up.

1169
00:48:16,059 --> 00:48:16,935
FOLDING LAUNDRY

1170
00:48:17,894 --> 00:48:18,812
TIRED

1171
00:48:20,397 --> 00:48:21,481
Done.

1172
00:48:21,565 --> 00:48:23,483
All done. Let's eat.

1173
00:48:23,567 --> 00:48:25,861
- Let's eat!
- Okay.

1174
00:48:25,944 --> 00:48:27,029
What did you make?

1175
00:48:27,112 --> 00:48:28,280
It's a stew.

1176
00:48:28,363 --> 00:48:30,574
- A stew again?
- Yes.

1177
00:48:30,657 --> 00:48:32,826
But you said
you'd make something delicious.

1178
00:48:32,909 --> 00:48:34,202
I can't make anything else.

1179
00:48:34,286 --> 00:48:35,579
What's wrong with you?

1180
00:48:35,662 --> 00:48:37,289
Just come try it.

1181
00:48:37,372 --> 00:48:38,707
TRYING IT FIRST

1182
00:48:38,790 --> 00:48:40,584
It's good. Come and try it.

1183
00:48:40,667 --> 00:48:42,878
Hurry up, or you won't get any food.

1184
00:48:42,961 --> 00:48:44,504
- Coming!
- Coming.

1185
00:48:44,588 --> 00:48:46,798
I have to wrap this up first, sir.

1186
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:48,759
Do it after lunch.

1187
00:48:48,842 --> 00:48:51,887
I'm dying over here.
I want double the pay.

1188
00:48:53,513 --> 00:48:55,057
- Boss.
- Yes?

1189
00:48:55,140 --> 00:48:57,601
Give us a bonus.

1190
00:48:58,685 --> 00:48:59,895
Where's the kimchi?

1191
00:48:59,978 --> 00:49:01,730
KIMCHI INSTEAD OF BONUSES

1192
00:49:01,813 --> 00:49:04,274
A stew again? Geez.

1193
00:49:05,359 --> 00:49:09,279
It's always either a stew or <i>ramyeon.</i>

1194
00:49:09,905 --> 00:49:11,615
I put in rice instead of noodles.

1195
00:49:11,698 --> 00:49:13,700
This rotten…

1196
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:16,411
I should just quit.

1197
00:49:16,495 --> 00:49:17,704
Try it.

1198
00:49:18,455 --> 00:49:20,248
Good work, everyone.

1199
00:49:20,332 --> 00:49:21,625
Thank you.

1200
00:49:21,708 --> 00:49:23,001
Let's eat this and…

1201
00:49:23,085 --> 00:49:23,960
12:50 P.M.

1202
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:25,462
It's spicy. Will you be okay, Zuha?

1203
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:27,881
- How spicy?
- Pretty spicy.

1204
00:49:27,964 --> 00:49:29,383
Pretty spicy?

1205
00:49:29,466 --> 00:49:30,592
Try it.

1206
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:32,427
Thank you for the food.

1207
00:49:32,511 --> 00:49:34,137
"Thank you for the food."

1208
00:49:37,432 --> 00:49:39,267
I'll just use my spoon
instead of chopsticks.

1209
00:49:39,351 --> 00:49:40,811
- Sure.
- Don't use chopsticks.

1210
00:49:40,894 --> 00:49:42,437
Don't use them.

1211
00:49:42,521 --> 00:49:43,897
There'll be more things to wash.

1212
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:47,818
USING CHOPSTICKS IS A WASTE

1213
00:49:47,901 --> 00:49:50,237
I bit the bullet
and gave you bowls to use too.

1214
00:49:52,656 --> 00:49:53,990
It's delicious.

1215
00:49:54,074 --> 00:49:55,242
That's all that matters then.

1216
00:49:58,286 --> 00:50:00,247
I feel like we've become farmers.

1217
00:50:00,330 --> 00:50:02,708
Clearing snow outside

1218
00:50:02,791 --> 00:50:04,376
and cleaning inside.

1219
00:50:05,419 --> 00:50:06,670
Seriously.

1220
00:50:06,753 --> 00:50:08,755
POT IS ALREADY ALMOST EMPTY

1221
00:50:10,382 --> 00:50:12,634
You worked so much
that you're scraping the pot.

1222
00:50:14,302 --> 00:50:16,012
We should eat the scorched rice too.

1223
00:50:19,558 --> 00:50:21,184
- Hey, Zuha.
- That's coal.

1224
00:50:21,268 --> 00:50:22,686
- The bottom's no good.
- Eat the top.

1225
00:50:22,769 --> 00:50:24,646
- The upper part.
- It's almost coal.

1226
00:50:24,730 --> 00:50:26,064
I can't tell you to eat that.

1227
00:50:26,148 --> 00:50:27,357
I'll just eat it.

1228
00:50:29,151 --> 00:50:30,277
She's not shying away.

1229
00:50:30,360 --> 00:50:31,987
She's not shying away now.

1230
00:50:32,529 --> 00:50:33,864
Honestly,

1231
00:50:34,531 --> 00:50:35,949
someone has to come now.

1232
00:50:36,032 --> 00:50:36,992
Who?

1233
00:50:37,075 --> 00:50:39,286
Anyone who'll help us.

1234
00:50:39,911 --> 00:50:42,664
I seriously hope someone comes to help.

1235
00:50:44,374 --> 00:50:45,667
Your phone's ringing.

1236
00:50:45,751 --> 00:50:47,210
- Where's it?
- Over there.

1237
00:50:47,294 --> 00:50:48,336
Be careful.

1238
00:50:50,839 --> 00:50:52,048
Where is it?

1239
00:50:53,842 --> 00:50:54,968
Hello?

1240
00:50:55,051 --> 00:50:57,345
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hello.

1241
00:50:57,429 --> 00:51:00,390
<i>- I'm checking in today.</i>
- Yes.

1242
00:51:00,474 --> 00:51:02,350
How many are in your party?

1243
00:51:02,434 --> 00:51:03,852
<i>- It's just me.</i>
- Just you?

1244
00:51:03,935 --> 00:51:07,230
Then, please come
to the address we'll send you.

1245
00:51:07,314 --> 00:51:09,065
1 GUEST IS EXPECTED TO CHECK IN

1246
00:51:09,149 --> 00:51:10,275
How many?

1247
00:51:10,358 --> 00:51:11,860
- One. It's a woman.
- One.

1248
00:51:11,943 --> 00:51:13,153
- I'll wrap up down here.
- Okay.

1249
00:51:13,236 --> 00:51:14,070
BACK TO WORK

1250
00:51:16,823 --> 00:51:18,408
- Another guest?
- Hello?

1251
00:51:18,492 --> 00:51:19,493
<i>Hello?</i>

1252
00:51:19,576 --> 00:51:22,954
<i>We're three high schoolers</i>
<i>checking in to Kian's B&B today.</i>

1253
00:51:23,038 --> 00:51:23,997
I see. Hello.

1254
00:51:24,080 --> 00:51:25,582
High schoolers.

1255
00:51:25,665 --> 00:51:27,292
- Three?
<i>- Yes.</i>

1256
00:51:27,375 --> 00:51:29,961
What time can we check in?

1257
00:51:30,045 --> 00:51:31,505
You can come at 4:00 p.m.

1258
00:51:31,588 --> 00:51:33,298
I'll send you the address.

1259
00:51:33,381 --> 00:51:34,841
Okay, thank you. Bye.

1260
00:51:34,925 --> 00:51:35,884
<i>Bye.</i>

1261
00:51:37,010 --> 00:51:39,012
- It's all on my hair.
- I didn't expect this much.

1262
00:51:39,095 --> 00:51:40,388
3 MORE GUESTS TO CHECK IN

1263
00:51:40,472 --> 00:51:42,724
There are already four more guests now.

1264
00:51:42,808 --> 00:51:44,726
I told you it'd be four more.

1265
00:51:44,810 --> 00:51:46,186
Did you prepare the rice?

1266
00:51:47,270 --> 00:51:49,147
THEY START PREPARING RICE FOR DINNER FIRST

1267
00:51:50,982 --> 00:51:53,360
We're out of water.
I have to go get another bottle.

1268
00:51:53,443 --> 00:51:55,862
I should throw out the recyclables.

1269
00:51:55,946 --> 00:51:58,740
THROWING OUT RECYCLABLES
BEFORE GUESTS COME

1270
00:51:58,824 --> 00:52:01,493
Zuha, could you bring
just these two outside?

1271
00:52:03,787 --> 00:52:05,080
STILL SNOWING HEAVILY

1272
00:52:05,163 --> 00:52:05,997
It's so cold.

1273
00:52:08,625 --> 00:52:10,085
Gosh, my feet are so cold.

1274
00:52:12,337 --> 00:52:13,463
My goodness.

1275
00:52:19,719 --> 00:52:22,347
- Zuha, can you carry this?
- Sorry?

1276
00:52:22,430 --> 00:52:23,515
THIS

1277
00:52:23,598 --> 00:52:24,599
Yes.

1278
00:52:25,141 --> 00:52:26,434
One, two, three.

1279
00:52:26,518 --> 00:52:29,604
STRONG ZUHA

1280
00:52:29,688 --> 00:52:31,147
IS OUT OF STRENGTH

1281
00:52:31,231 --> 00:52:32,691
It's like the Arctic here.

1282
00:52:33,859 --> 00:52:35,277
Gosh, hold on!

1283
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:36,862
The wind is so strong.

1284
00:52:40,490 --> 00:52:41,992
- Give it to me.
- Where do I put it?

1285
00:52:42,075 --> 00:52:43,660
- I'll just…
- Yeah, there.

1286
00:52:45,370 --> 00:52:47,789
Are you working her hard
because she's the youngest?

1287
00:52:47,873 --> 00:52:49,541
Well, we did it together.

1288
00:52:49,624 --> 00:52:52,627
Goodness. Our youngest is working so hard.

1289
00:52:55,881 --> 00:52:57,340
- Lift it up?
- Yeah, hold on.

1290
00:52:57,424 --> 00:52:58,675
THE BOSS WILL MOVE THE WATER UP

1291
00:53:00,802 --> 00:53:02,304
Can you do it with one hand?

1292
00:53:02,387 --> 00:53:03,889
I don't think it'll work.

1293
00:53:05,432 --> 00:53:07,726
Wait. Hold on.

1294
00:53:07,809 --> 00:53:09,519
RETREATS

1295
00:53:11,354 --> 00:53:12,647
Can you take this up?

1296
00:53:12,731 --> 00:53:14,733
- Push it all the way up.
- Put it on your head.

1297
00:53:14,816 --> 00:53:16,401
Push it up all the way. Wait.

1298
00:53:16,484 --> 00:53:18,111
If you drop it…

1299
00:53:18,194 --> 00:53:20,238
JUN-HO CARRIES IT UP

1300
00:53:21,072 --> 00:53:22,282
We did it.

1301
00:53:23,366 --> 00:53:25,243
PANTING

1302
