1698
01:10:46,492 --> 01:10:48,452
SNU's School of Earth
and Environmental Sciences.

1699
01:10:48,535 --> 01:10:50,120
- Earth and Environmental Sciences?
- Yes.

1700
01:10:50,204 --> 01:10:52,248
- And you?
- I want to major in astrophysics.

1701
01:10:52,331 --> 01:10:53,165
Astrophysics?

1702
01:10:53,249 --> 01:10:55,668
They're similar.
Earth science and astrophysics.

1703
01:10:55,751 --> 01:10:58,045
We're members of the astronomy club.

1704
01:10:58,128 --> 01:10:59,838
- The same club.
- The astronomy club?

1705
01:10:59,922 --> 01:11:02,841
Yes, so all our stuff over there
are the telescopes we brought.

1706
01:11:02,925 --> 01:11:03,759
Telescopes?

1707
01:11:03,842 --> 01:11:06,470
A total lunar eclipse
will take place tomorrow.

1708
01:11:06,553 --> 01:11:08,347
- A total lunar eclipse tomorrow?
- Yes.

1709
01:11:08,430 --> 01:11:10,808
Then, which one will be covered?
The moon or the sun?

1710
01:11:10,891 --> 01:11:14,395
It's a lunar eclipse.
And "lunar" means "moon," right?

1711
01:11:14,478 --> 01:11:17,231
It happens
when the Earth's shadow covers the moon.

1712
01:11:17,314 --> 01:11:19,275
So, they overlap?

1713
01:11:19,358 --> 01:11:20,192
Yes.

1714
01:11:20,276 --> 01:11:23,237
One of the characteristics
is that the moon looks red.

1715
01:11:23,320 --> 01:11:25,990
THE THREE CAME TO DAEGWALLYEONG
TO OBSERVE STARS

1716
01:11:26,073 --> 01:11:27,908
The moon will be slowly covered…

1717
01:11:27,992 --> 01:11:29,159
Will we be able to see it?

1718
01:11:29,952 --> 01:11:32,162
It's snowing,
so will it be visible tomorrow?

1719
01:11:33,497 --> 01:11:35,332
We should check the forecast.

1720
